(Regression test for bug #48: the three write macros issued their write
syscall and never looked at the result, and `Write` itself never touched the
error flag, so from inside Vox a write that did not happen was
indistinguishable from one that did. `Read from` a handle whose open failed
was silent in the same way, where `Read line from` the identical handle
already set the flag.)

(The control: a write that succeeds must NOT fire the handler.)
open a file for writing called 'the good file' at "/tmp/vox_test_write_errors.txt".
Write "written" to 'the good file'.
On error print "BUG: a successful write fired the error handler", exit 1.
Write a newline to 'the good file'.
On error print "BUG: a successful newline write fired the error handler", exit 1.
a buffer called payload is "payload".
Write payload to 'the good file'.
On error print "BUG: a successful buffer write fired the error handler", exit 1.
Close 'the good file'.
print "the successful writes did not fire the handler".

(A full device accepts the open and fails every write with ENOSPC - a real
failure on a valid, writable handle, not a bad descriptor.)
open a file for writing called 'the full device' at "/dev/full".
Write "x" to 'the full device'.
On error print "the write to a full device set the error flag".
Write a newline to 'the full device'.
On error print "the newline write to a full device set the error flag".
Write payload to 'the full device'.
On error print "the buffer write to a full device set the error flag".
Close 'the full device'.

(A handle opened for reading is not writable.)
open a file for reading called 'the reading handle' at "/tmp/vox_test_write_errors.txt".
Write "x" to 'the reading handle'.
On error print "the write to a read-only handle set the error flag".
Close 'the reading handle'.

(A closed handle's descriptor is no longer open.)
open a file for writing called 'the closed handle' at "/tmp/vox_test_write_errors_closed.txt".
Close 'the closed handle'.
Write "x" to 'the closed handle'.
On error print "the write to a closed handle set the error flag".

(A handle whose open failed carries a negative descriptor. Both read forms and
the write must agree that using it is an error.)
open a file for reading called missing at "/tmp/vox_test_write_errors_absent.txt".
On error print "the failed open set the error flag".
a buffer called chunk is 16 bytes in size.
Read from missing into chunk.
On error print "Read from a failed handle set the error flag".
Read line from missing into chunk.
On error print "Read line from a failed handle set the error flag".
Write "x" to missing.
On error print "the write to a failed handle set the error flag".

Delete the file "/tmp/vox_test_write_errors.txt".
Delete the file "/tmp/vox_test_write_errors_closed.txt".
